2026-09-02: Added windT_ic_approach: phenomenological T_ic from L/Ledd (Done et al. 2018), with a new T_ic output column. Fixed BasicWind R_IC_ to guard missing T_ic and recompute under Done2018. Added undocumented Dubus2001 irradiation_type for comparison; reworked Dubus2019 irradiation_type per feedback and applied radiation-pressure correction to R_IC in the Dubus2019 branch only. Documented T_ic/R_IC output columns and cross-referenced them from --windT_ic help text.

2026-09-03: Fixed a hard crash in the wind outer-boundary solver (now fails gracefully); collapsed per-retry stdout spam into one summary line per solve. Added a posteriori Cirr diagnostic columns for scatter_dependent and Dubus2019, plus a standalone C_irr_direct diagnostic column.

2026-09-04: Added Mdot_wind_Dubus2019 diagnostic output column. Documented the Dubus2019 comparison tools in a temporary README section.

2026-09-08: Fixed citation (Done et al. 2018 is actually Tomaru & Takahashi, MNRAS 473, 838). Fixed crash: Mdot_wind_Dubus2019 now skips instead of throwing. Smoothed the Done2018 T_ic transition and made wind launch radius tunable. Documented --wind_Irr_ang_distribution in the Compton-heated wind README section. Applied the Dubus2019 R_IC radiation-pressure correction to the real wind physics (not just diagnostics).

2026-09-09: Integrated Compton wind mass loss over the whole disc, not just the hot zone. Added Cirr_scatter_Rtid diagnostic output column.

2026-09-29: Traced Cirr_Dubus2019 diagnostic column (freddi_state.cpp Cirr_Dubus2019()) for the user: it's a disc-wide constant, not evaluated at Rhot or Rtid directly — its R_in wind-launch radius is 0.2*R_IC (Compton radius), and its Mdot_wind() integrates over the full disc grid out to Nx()-1, which is the fixed outer disc edge (Rtid by default), not the moving hot-zone/cooling-front radius Rhot. No code changes made.

2026-09-29: Explained for the user why Mdot_wind_cold coincides with Mdot_wind_Dubus2019 in the "Mdot" panel for wind_Dubus_fig3.ini (test_Cirr_scatter_Tic_var/freddi.dat): (1) that config uses windtype=Woods1996 + windT_ic_approach=Done2018, which already applies the same Dubus(2019) R_IC radiation-pressure correction and launch-radius cutoff as the Mdot_wind_Dubus2019() diagnostic, so Mdot_wind_Dubus2019 ≈ true Mdot_wind() (total) almost exactly; (2) with windR_launch_factor=1e-3, the Woods1996 wind-loss density rises so steeply toward large R that as soon as any cold zone exists (Rhot<Rout), the cold-zone contribution (Mdot_wind_cold) dominates the total within a few days, so Mdot_wind_cold ≈ Mdot_wind ≈ Mdot_wind_Dubus2019 for most of the light curve. No code changes made.

2026-09-29: Verified Cirr_Dubus2019() (freddi_state.cpp) against Dubus et al. (2019) Eq. (10): the sigma_T/m_I, Mdot_w, and Rin=0.2*R_IC terms all matched, but the paper's v_w ("mass-weighted wind outflow rate", text below Eq. 10) was implemented as a single-radius proxy v_esc(Rin)=sqrt(2GM/Rin) rather than a true mass weighted average. Confirmed windR_launch_factor only affects R_wind_inner_launch_radius(), used solely by Woods1996ShieldsApproxWind::update() (the real --windtype=Woods1996 physics) and the Mdot_wind_Dubus2019() diagnostic -- it was NOT read by Cirr_Dubus2019() at all. For wind_Dubus_fig3.ini (windR_launch_factor=1e-3), found Rin=0.2*R_IC (~2.38e11 cm) actually exceeds Rout (~1.0e11 cm), so nearly all of the simulated Mdot_wind() originates well inside the paper's own Rin -- the old v_w=v_esc(Rin) proxy did not represent where the wind mass actually is. Fixed: v_w is now dMdot_wind_dh(i)-weighted average of v_esc()[i] over the same (first(), Nx()-1) range as Mdot_wind(), automatically staying consistent with whatever windR_launch_factor produced; added a Mdot_wind()<=0 guard (0/0 case). Rin itself left at the paper's fixed 0.2*R_IC (not tied to windR_launch_factor), per Eq. 10/Eq. 4's own definition. Diagnostic-only column, no effect on simulated physics. Verified the change compiles and links cleanly (cmake+make freddi-exe in a scratch build dir); did not reproduce a full run to compare old vs. new Cirr_Dubus2019 values numerically (wind_Dubus_fig3.ini's config-chaining with freddi.ini's quasistat F0 needs the same wrapper workflow noted in the 2026-09-23 entry; a direct CLI reconstruction hit an unrelated "Rout <= Rin" initial-condition mismatch, not a regression from this change).

