2026-09-23: Reconstructed the fig3 plot workflow for 4U1543-47_freddi_wind_Dubus_fig3.pdf from ~/.bash_history and freddi.dat's `# config=` header (freddi run with --config=<ini> then `FREDDI_GNUPLOT_BACKEND=1 $PERLTOOLSDIR/show.pl fredevol all freddi.dat`, which auto-names the PDF from plot.ini's src + the config filename). Reran the same workflow for fig6 (wind_Dubus_fig6.ini, Mdot0=2.9e+18) against the current (Sep 9) physics code, regenerating 4U1543-47_freddi_wind_Dubus_fig6.pdf in /home/glipunova/galja/rabota/freddi/test_Cirr_scatter_Tic_var/. Note: Mdot0=2e19 fails immediately (Rout <= Rin) for this config; the 2.9e18 run still terminates early at t~204.5 days of the requested 1000 (disc equation fails to converge), though further than the prior data's t~38 days.

2026-09-29: At the user's request, changed Cirr_Dubus2019()'s v_w mass-weighting from integrating dMdot_wind_dh(i) over h (specific angular momentum) to integrating over r directly: added a local dMdot_wind_dr(i) = dMdot_wind_dh(i) * GM/(2h) lambda (Jacobian dh/dr for h=sqrt(GM r)), and both the v_esc-weighted numerator and the normalizing denominator (Mdot_w_dr) are now trapz(R(), ..., first(), Nx()-1) instead of trapz(h(), ...). The Mdot_w used in the final C formula itself is unchanged (still Mdot_wind()/h-based, matching the rest of the codebase). Verified the change compiles cleanly (cmake+make cpp/src/freddi_state.o in a scratch build dir, cleaned up after). Also noted cmake-build-dev3/freddi is stale (built 2026-09-09), predating 5 commits' worth of changes to freddi_state.cpp/output.cpp (Cirr_scatter_Rtid, full-disc Mdot_wind integration, Dubus2019 R_IC correction to the real wind physics, citation fix, Mdot_wind_Dubus2019 crash fix) plus this session's Cirr_Dubus2019 edits -- needs a rebuild before results from it can be trusted.

2026-10-01: Committed the pending Cirr_Dubus2019 mass-weighted-v_w change (commit cfeaf8c) to close out prior work before starting new development. Researched how to add a new radial (--fulldata) output column tau_perp_wind(r): columns are registered as {name, unit, description, lambda} entries in FreddiFileOutput::initializeDiskStructureFields() (cpp/src/output.cpp ~315-326), automatically inherited by freddi-ns via ns_output.cpp. Found the needed physics already exists as Column_density_wind() (cpp/src/freddi_state.cpp ~712-727, Sigma_wind = Mdot_wind_running/(4 pi R v_wind)); tau_perp_wind is simply scattering_opacity * Column_density_wind(i), matching the formula already used inline in Cirr_scatter_dependent() and documented in the --irradiation_type help text (cpp/src/options.cpp:343). Planned follow-up additions of the same shape: tau_perp_corona (from a dynamically-stable corona), tau_r_wind and tau_r_corona (optical depth along the disc, i.e. radial rather than perpendicular). No physics/output code changes made yet for tau_perp_wind itself -- pending user go-ahead on the proposed edit (new FreddiState::tau_perp_wind() accessor + opt_str_ cache entry + output.cpp column registration).

2026-10-01: Implemented tau_perp_wind(r) as a new --fulldata radial output column. Added FreddiState::tau_perp_wind() (cpp/src/freddi_state.cpp, right after Column_density_wind()) computing scattering_opacity * Column_density_wind(i) with the same lazy opt_str_ caching pattern; added the tau_perp_wind cache slot and public accessor declaration to cpp/include/freddi_state.hpp; registered the column ("tau_perp_wind", unit "dimensionless") in FreddiFileOutput::initializeDiskStructureFields() (cpp/src/output.cpp), so it also appears automatically in freddi-ns radial output. Rebuilt freddi-exe in cmake-build-dev3 (clean compile, only pre-existing unrelated deprecation warnings). Verified numerically with a short run (wind_Dubus_fig3.ini config, --irradiation_type=scatter_dependent, --time=0.5, --fulldata, in a scratch dir, deleted after): the outer-radius value of tau_perp_wind in the radial file matched scattering_opacity(0.34) * Sigma_wind from the main freddi.dat output to full precision (1.31823588774e-11 both ways), and was consistent with the existing Cirr_scatter_out diagnostic (etaX * tau_perp_wind/2). Not yet committed -- pending user review. Next planned additions (same pattern): tau_perp_corona, tau_r_wind, tau_r_corona.

2026-10-02: Added tau_perp_corona(r) radial (--fulldata) output column implementing Ostriker, McKee & Klein (1991, ApJ 377, 593) Eq. (47) with Xi_tilde = 0.65*(T_ic/1e8 K)^-3/2 (Eq. 29b), xi = R/R_IC, T_mb/T_ic = 1, f = exp(-(tau_parallel_corona+tau_parallel_wind)) (only f_dir of Eq. 18 for now). tau_parallel_corona()/tau_parallel_wind() are placeholders returning 0 (f=1). Zero for wind types without T_ic. Files: freddi_state.hpp/.cpp, output.cpp. freddi-exe compiles cleanly; not numerically tested or committed. Assumption to confirm: Ticr -> T_ic in units of 1e8 K.

2026-10-02: Added reference to OMK (1991) Eq. (55) (same tau_perp expression as Eq. 47) in the tau_perp_corona code comment and output column description. No other docs mention the column. Rebuilt freddi-exe cleanly.

2026-10-02: Implemented tau_r_wind(r) and tau_r_corona(r) radial (--fulldata) columns, and wired them into tau_perp_corona via tau_parallel_wind/corona (replacing the zero placeholders). New FreddiState::R_hc() solves OMK Eq. (20) L/(4 pi R^2) = 2 Qvis (Qvis = sigma_SB*Tph_vis^4 = 3 Fvis omegaK/(8 pi R^2)), outermost crossing on the grid, log-interpolated. tau_r_corona = tau_perp(f=1)*xi^1/2/xi_hc for R>=R_hc, else 0 (= l/(Xi_tilde xi_hc), constant); tau_r_wind = kappa_es * int_{R_launch}^R Mdot_wind_running/(4 pi R^2 v_wind) dR with R_launch = R_wind_inner_launch_radius(wind_->R_IC()) (0 for wind types without R_launch_factor). tau_perp_corona = f*l/(Xi_tilde sqrt(xi)) with f=exp(-(tau_r_corona+tau_r_wind)), zero for R<R_hc or R_IC<=0. R_IC taken as wind_->R_IC() (Dubus-corrected under Done2018), per user. Code comments + column descriptions state that super-Eddington/magnetic winds are ignored. Test run (wind_Dubus_fig6.ini, Mdot0=2.9e18, t=3d, scratch dir, deleted): tau_r_corona = 106 for R>=~5e7 cm (R<R_hc: 0), so f~e^-106 and tau_perp_corona ~1e-47 -- corona is effectively fully self-attenuated in that model. Not committed.

2026-10-02: Per user decision, corona quantities (tau_r_corona, tau_perp_corona, xi_hc) now use the genuine R_IC = GM mu m_p/(kB T_ic) via new FreddiState::R_IC_corona(), WITHOUT the Dubus (1-sqrt2 L/Ledd) correction; tau_r_wind still uses wind_->R_IC() (corrected under windT_ic_approach=Done2018). Rebuilt freddi-exe cleanly. Found (not fixed, reported to user): for L/Ledd>1/sqrt2 under Done2018, wind R_iC_from_T_ic() goes negative and Shields/Woods wind update() then yields NaN/garbage (pow of negative xi), not a clean "wind everywhere".

2026-10-02: Clamped the Dubus (1-sqrt2 L/Ledd) correction factor in R_iC_from_T_ic() to >=1e-6 (floor on R_IC relative to uncorrected value) so L/Ledd>=1/sqrt2 no longer gives negative R_IC/NaN in Shields/Woods winds. Rebuilt freddi-exe cleanly; not run at L/Ledd>1/sqrt2, not committed.

2026-10-02: Radial (--fulldata) dump in output.cpp now always covers the whole grid (first..Nx()-1, up to Rtid) instead of only up to Rhot unless --colddiskflux. Rebuilt; verified a short run (scratch, deleted): 1000 rows to R~1e12 cm. Observed: Tvis (Tph_vis) and the corona columns (tau_r_corona/tau_perp_corona loop to last()) are 0 beyond Rhot; tau_*_wind are filled over the whole grid. Not committed.

2026-10-02: R_hc() now evaluates Qvis = 3 F omega_K/(8 pi R^2) from F() over the whole grid (not Tph_vis, which is only filled to Rhot), scanning first..Nx()-1; tau_r_corona and tau_perp_corona loops extended from last() to Nx()-1. Verified (scratch run, deleted): corona columns are now non-zero out to R~1e12 cm (R_hc~5e7 cm, tau_r_corona=126 at t=3d). Not committed.

2026-10-02: tau_r_corona changed to OMK Appendix G Eq. G.2: tau_par = (L/Ledd)/Xi_tilde * (R/Height)^2 (f=1, hot optically thin corona, h_x~0), zero inside R_hc or where Height()<=0; tau_perp_corona skips the same nodes. Test (fig6, 3d): tau_r_corona now varies with R (2.6 -> 1.1 in the hot disc). Issue: beyond Rhot Height()=h2rcold*R=0 for this config, so both corona columns are 0 there -- asked user how to get z_disk in the cold zone. Also told user: R_IC (wind, Dubus-corrected) is in freddi.dat; the genuine R_IC_corona is not output. Not committed.

2026-10-02: Added static-corona cut-off to tau_r_corona and tau_perp_corona: zero for R > 0.1*R_IC (constant xi_max_static_corona in freddi_state.cpp), R_IC genuine (R_IC_corona(), no Dubus correction); documented in code comments and the tau_perp_corona/tau_r_corona column descriptions. Verified (scratch, --h2rcold=0.05, deleted): last non-zero node 1.61e11 cm vs 0.1*R_IC~1.62e11 cm. Not committed.

2026-10-02: Corona tau_par (G.2) in the cold zone beyond Rhot now uses z_disk = 0.001*R (constant z_disk_to_R_cold_corona, new FreddiState::z_disk_corona(i): Height() up to Rhot, 0.001 R beyond); Height() itself unchanged. Documented in code comment and column description. Test (fig6, 3d): tau_r_corona=2210 beyond Rhot (up to 0.1 R_IC), so tau_perp_corona underflows to 0 there (f=exp(-2210)); both 0 beyond 0.1 R_IC. Not committed.

2026-10-03: Changed cold-zone (beyond Rhot) corona z_disk from 0.001*R to 0.01*R (z_disk_to_R_cold_corona, comment and column description updated). Rebuilt freddi-exe cleanly; not rerun, not committed.

2026-10-05: Reversed the 0.1*R_IC corona cut-off and the cold-zone z_disk=0.01*R (removed xi_max_static_corona, z_disk_to_R_cold_corona, z_disk_corona()). tau_r_corona and tau_perp_corona are now computed from R_hc up to Rhot (i<=last()) using Height(); beyond Rhot the cold disc is in the shadow -> 0. Comments/column descriptions updated. Rebuilt cleanly, short fig6 run checked (scratch, deleted). Not committed.

2026-10-05: Corona columns: removed the Rhot cut; shadowing is now evaluated independently via the existing FreddiState::Shadow() (1 where H/R < running max of H/R, i.e. shadowed by the disc itself); tau_r_corona and tau_perp_corona skip nodes with Shadow()>0 over the whole grid. Restored the cold-zone z_disk=0.01*R rule (z_disk_to_R_cold_corona, z_disk_corona(i): Height() up to Rhot, 0.01 R beyond). Test fig6 3d: with h2rcold=0 (default) the cold zone is shadowed -> 0; with --h2rcold=0.05 some cold nodes get tau_r_corona=22 (0.01R rule), others still 0 (Shadow() flips on rounding when H/R is exactly constant, existing behaviour). Not committed.

2026-10-05: Added scalar freddi.dat column tau_r_corona_RIC = tau_r_corona (G.2) evaluated directly at the genuine R_IC (FreddiState::tau_r_corona_at_R_IC(); z_disk = interpolated Height() if R_IC<=Rhot else 0.01 R_IC; 0 if R_IC<R_hc or no T_ic; Shadow NOT taken into account -- user will decide later whether to include it). Verified (fig6, 3d, scratch deleted): 30.4 -> 22.1 over t=0..3 d; at t=3 matches the cold-zone grid value 22.106. Not committed.

2026-10-05: Added scalar freddi.dat column tau_r_corona_Rhot = tau_r_corona()[last()] (grid value at Rhot, so Shadow and R_hc cuts apply). Verified in a short fig6 run (scratch deleted). Not committed.

2026-10-05: Added freddi.dat columns R_Fmax (radius of max Fvis over the whole grid, new FreddiState::i_Fmax()) and tau_r_corona_Fmax (grid value of tau_r_corona there; R_hc and Shadow cuts apply). Confirmed to user that R_IC is a freddi.dat column (the wind R_IC, Dubus-corrected under Done2018; genuine R_IC is not stored). Verified in a short fig6 run (scratch deleted). Not committed.

2026-10-05: i_Fmax() (columns R_Fmax, tau_r_corona_Fmax) now takes the F maximum over the hot zone first()..last() instead of the whole grid; tau_r_corona_Rhot kept. Not committed.

2026-11-10: Analysed tau_r_evol.pdf (test_Cirr_scatter_Tic_var, t=54.25 d): tau_r_corona (~0.65 at 1e11 cm, OMK G.2 static-corona estimate, ignores flaring only in cold zone: 0.01 R) vs tau_r_wind (~1e-6, cumulative Mdot_wind_running/(4 pi R^2 v_esc)) differ because corona density would need ~3e20 g/s at v_esc (>> Mdot_wind 1.9e19, Mdot 2e18) -> bound static corona, not an outflow. Corona drop at ~1.2e11 cm is the Shadow() mask (H/R decreasing), not Rhot (~3e11). No code changes. Per user request: added antropic.log and messages.txt to the repo, committed the tau_perp_corona/tau_r_wind/tau_r_corona work and pushed branch galja-dev3-Tic.

2026-11-11: Traced tau_r_evol.pdf: made by `show.pl fredevol tau_r_t radial` (laptop copy galja_laptop/galja/prog/perl/fredevol.pl:2421; muses PERLTOOLSDIR copy lacks it). Checked tau_r_corona against Ostriker+91 (galja_laptop/galja/rabota/papers/1543_winds/pubs/Ostriker+91.pdf): it is OMK Eq. 45 with h_x=0, i.e. the integral source->disc surface tau(xi)=int_{xi_min}^{xi} n sigma R_IC dxi (Eqs. 35, 39, 44), dominated by xi_min~(H/R)^2; NOT OMK tau_parallel (Eqs. 48-49) and NOT local. "Appendix G, G.2" citation did not exist in the paper (user does not remember its origin): corrected comments in freddi_state.cpp and output.cpp help texts; column names unchanged. Built OK. Not committed.

2026-11-11: Restored the "G.2" label in tau_r_corona comment and help texts with a WARNING (unverified, OMK91 has no Appendix G). Checked Eq. 40 exact (h_x=0: xi_min=(H/R)^2, tau=tau45*(1-xi_min/xi)) for freddi_217.dat (t=54.25 d, T_ic=5.3e6 K, R_IC=1.7e12 cm, Mx=9, mu=0.62 assumed): for R <~ 3e9 cm xi < (H/R)^2, i.e. corona scale height < disc height, OMK thick-corona assumption fails and exact tau=0, while code (Eq. 45) gives 1-3; at 1e10 cm Eq. 45 overestimates by 1.5x, at >=5e10 cm by <10%. No code fix applied yet. Not committed.

2026-11-11: Switched tau_r_corona to the exact h_x=0 solution of OMK91 Eqs. 39-40: tau=(L/Ledd)/Xi_tilde*max(0,(R/z_disk)^2-R_IC/R) (was Eq. 45 = "G.2", warning kept); tau_r_corona_RIC accordingly max(0,(R_IC/z)^2-1); docs/help updated. Verified by rerunning test_Cirr_scatter_Tic_var to t=54.25 d in scratch: grid, Height, tau_r_wind unchanged; tau_r_corona now zero for R<2.8e9 cm (was 1-3), 0.58 vs 0.89 at 1e10, 0.62 vs 0.66 at 1e11; tau_perp_corona rises in the inner disc (0.43 vs 0.026 at 3e7 cm) since f_dir=exp(-tau) no longer suppresses it. Not committed.

2026-11-11: tau_perp_corona now also zero where R/R_IC <= (z_disk/R)^2 (corona scale height not above disc semi-height; OMK Eq. 47 assumes h_c > h_d) -- same cut as tau_r_corona; WARNING in comment and help text. Rerun at 54.25 d: tau_perp_corona nonzero 2.78e9..1.14e11 cm (same as tau_r_corona). Tests pass. Not committed. Discussed: tau_r_corona integral has no upper cut at R_IC (OMK/Begelman+83: static corona xi<~0.1, wind xi>~1); in this run R_launch=1e-3 R_IC=1.7e9 cm so corona and wind overlap in f_dir. Perl plot tools: galja_laptop/galja/prog/perl is a git clone (github gvlipunova/perl-plot-tools, branch gnuplot-backend, 9 commits ahead of last-fetched origin, uncommitted tau_r_t/tau_perp_t work); muses PERLTOOLSDIR (/homes/glipunova/galja/prog/perl) is not a git repo, older, but holds ~30 untracked scripts (fredevol_specific_*.pl etc.). No GitHub credentials/gh on muses.

