2026-11-13: At the user's request (for the fitadisc fitting layer): (1) the "Disc equation: needed N retries of right_bc" summary in cpp/src/nonlinear_diffusion.cpp now goes to stderr instead of stdout, so --stdout output stays clean; (2) new freddi.dat column bc_retries [count]: nonlinear_diffusion_nonuniform_wind_1_2() got an optional trailing `int* bc_retries` argument (max of the retry counts of the solves it is called for), CurrentState got `int bc_retries`, FreddiEvolution::step() resets it to 0 before the solve and both call sites (plain and the Brent loop of nonlinear_diffusion_outer_condition_depends_Mdotin) pass &current_.bc_retries; registered in output.cpp before Rfront_Rhot. Build note: the make targets are freddi-exe and freddi-ns-exe (`make freddi` matches the binary file and does nothing). Verified on the 1543 HXMT set-up (wind.ini, alpha 0.3, Mdot0 1.5e19, 71 d): all other columns identical to the previous binary (relative difference 0), bc_retries = 1..9 at t = 69-71 d, 7 retry lines on stderr, none on stdout. Still on stdout: the "(W) RESULT factor ..." printf in freddi_evolution.cpp:107 (not changed). Not committed.

2026-11-13: Resolution study of the right_bc retries (1543 HXMT wind+DIM set-up, alpha 0.3, Mdot0 1.5e19, 71 d; scratch runs, nothing kept): over Nx = 500..4000 and tau = 0.355..0.044 d the retries/failures occur when tau is small relative to the grid step (Nx 500: all tau below default fail; Nx 1000: clean at tau/2, "Disc equation failed to converge" at tau/4 and tau/8, i.e. 100 retries reached; Nx 2000: fails only at tau/8; Nx 4000: clean at all tau). The retries are therefore a discretisation effect at the outer boundary cell, not an inadmissible boundary condition. Within 20-70 d the default (Nx 1000, tau 0.355) differs from the finest run (Nx 4000, tau 0.044) by 1.0% in Mdot (median), Nx 1000 tau/2 by 0.4%, Nx 2000 tau/4 by 0.1%; the collapse time near 70 d moves with resolution. Costs: 1.2 s, 9 s (Nx 2000 tau/2), 98 s (Nx 4000 tau/8). Suggestion recorded: treat bc_retries > 0 as a request for finer resolution, and review the one-sided discretisation of the Neumann condition in the last cell (a[last], c0[last], frac[last] with the 0.5 factor in nonlinear_diffusion_nonuniform_wind_1_2). No code changes.

2026-11-13: At the user's request, replaced the 1%-retry loop in nonlinear_diffusion_nonuniform_wind_1_2 (cpp/src/nonlinear_diffusion.cpp) by an exact clamp with reporting. New static helper solve_with_clamped_outer_bc(): in every Picard iteration the solution is affine in the outer boundary condition bc (y_i = yA_i + yB_i*bc, computed by one extra back-substitution), so the admissible range of bc (y >= 0 everywhere) is known exactly; a requested bc outside it is clamped to the bound times (1 - 1e-3), moving toward zero only; if even bc = 0 gives negative F (interior problem) -> DiscEqFailException with a stderr message. The back-substitution for the final y uses the original formula, so unclamped solves are bit-identical to the old code. Non-convergence of the Picard iteration (maxiter 100) is retried at most 3 times with bc halved, each reported on stderr, then DiscEqFailException. Reporting: optional trailing args `int* bc_clamped` (max over the step of the number of clamped iterations) and `double* bc_factor` (min over the step of effective/requested bc) replace bc_retries everywhere (CurrentState, accessors, both call sites, reset in FreddiEvolution::step()); freddi.dat columns bc_clamped [count] and bc_factor [float]; one stderr line per clamped solve "Disc equation: outer boundary condition clamped from A to B (factor f) in n iterations to keep F >= 0". Verification on the 1543 HXMT set-up: default run (Nx 1000, tau 0.355) bit-identical to the Oct-5 binary in all 201 rows (clamps only acted inside Brent's exploration at t = 69-71 d, factors 0.99-0.90); tau x Nx grid: clean runs unchanged and same timings; the runs that previously died with "Disc equation failed to converge" (Nx 500 at tau <= 0.1775, Nx 1000 at tau <= 0.08875, Nx 2000 at tau 0.044) now end instead with the physical collapse Rout <= Rin at 53-69 d (clamp factors down to 0.15-0.25, one non-convergence retry in Nx 1000 tau 0.08875); Nx 4000 is clean at every tau. So the early collapse at coarse grid + small step is a resolution effect that the clamp makes visible instead of masking. Not committed.
